  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Bagrus bajad (Fabricius, 1775)</li><li><strong>Common name:</strong> Black Nile Catfish</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Nile River, Egypt.</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 112 cm (44.1\") SL</li><li><strong>Identification:</strong> Distinguished in having dorsal fin rays produced into short filaments, predorsal distance 2.4-2.6 times in standard length and head width 1.7-2.2 times in head length.</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Least Concern (last assessed 2020).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Africa: Nile River, Lake Chad, Niger and Sénégal River, Lakes Mobutu (Lake Albert) and Turkana. Reported from Sanaga River basin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Occurs in water less than 12 m deep.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.4 - 8.0</li><li>Temperature: 21.0-27.0°C (69.8-80.6°F)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Provide plenty of driftwood as hiding places.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Preys on small fish, particularly Alestes spp., also feeds on insects, crustaceans, mollusks, vegetable matter. In the aquarium it readily feeds on live/frozen foods and other prepared foods such as pellets. Will eat smaller fishes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Although young fish can be kept with other fish of equal or larger sizes, adult fish are aggressive and should be kept alone.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Males have an elongate genital papilla in front of the anal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Not reported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1110",
      "html": "<p>Descriptiones animalium (Forsskål), pp 66, xiii.</p>"
    }
  ],
